.","C":"Myself is singular and matches I, not we.","D":"The ordinary plural reflexive for we is ourselves."}}},{"id":"922776a1-1455-5a29-ae53-8f0c49af0c3e","topicSlug":"reflexive-reciprocal","level":"B1","prompt":"“The two assistants helped each other to restore the old portrait.” What does “each other” show?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Neither assistant received help."},{"id":"B","text":"Each assistant helped the other assistant."},{"id":"C","text":"Each assistant helped only themselves."},{"id":"D","text":"Only one assistant received help."}],"answerId":"B","hint":"A reciprocal action goes **from A to B and from B to A**.","explanation":"**Each other** expresses a reciprocal action between the two assistants.","keywords":["reciprocal-meaning"],"skill":"reciprocal-meaning","contextKey":"reflexive-reciprocal-2","fingerprint":"0bd9765e2c9b9ddac7dda468d789f17ea0d4dd1cfa66f04c5bd2c7fd8011098d","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reflexive"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["A reciprocal action goes **from A to B and from B to A**.","**Each other** expresses a reciprocal action between the two assistants.","Choose **Each assistant helped the other assistant.**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This contradicts helped each other.","B":"**Each other** expresses a reciprocal action between the two assistants.","C":"That would be reflexive, not reciprocal.","D":"The stated reciprocal relationship goes both ways."}}},{"id":"af27746a-5fa7-51aa-aa6c-6bc00afb6ed7","topicSlug":"reflexive-reciprocal","level":"B1","prompt":"“The supervisor asked Sam and ____ to restore the old portrait.” Choose the standard object pronoun for the speaker.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"I"},{"id":"B","text":"myself"},{"id":"C","text":"mine"},{"id":"D","text":"me"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Test the role without the other name: **asked me**.","explanation":"Sam and **me** is the object of asked; removing Sam and leaves asked me.","keywords":["ordinary-object-pronoun"],"skill":"ordinary-object-pronoun","contextKey":"reflexive-reciprocal-2","fingerprint":"c6bf8caecde312cbc4ad621262d8c450b8b849f5ff92eff7068fb10aae8fa352","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reflexive"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Test the role without the other name: **asked me**.","Sam and **me** is the object of asked; removing Sam and leaves asked me.","Choose **me**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"I is a subject pronoun, but the phrase is the object of asked.","B":"The subject is the supervisor, so myself has no matching subject for an ordinary reflexive use.","C":"Mine is possessive and cannot be the person object here.","D":"Sam and **me** is the object of asked; removing Sam and leaves asked me."}}},{"id":"52d24c6d-bd53-5e31-ae02-05f473d33d9d","topicSlug":"reflexive-reciprocal","level":"B1","prompt":"“She measured the garden fence by ____.” Choose the matching reflexive.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"her"},{"id":"B","text":"herself"},{"id":"C","text":"himself"},{"id":"D","text":"themselves"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Match the reflexive to **she**, and recognise **by herself**.","explanation":"**Herself** matches the feminine singular subject she; by herself means without help or company.","keywords":["singular-reflexive"],"skill":"singular-reflexive","contextKey":"reflexive-reciprocal-3","fingerprint":"df2c161757f6038d4900346fab0d0d9b0d478e0e4e7c604e4ed574fa86c28056","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reflexive"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Match the reflexive to **she**, and recognise **by herself**.","**Herself** matches the feminine singular subject she; by herself means without help or company.","Choose **herself**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"After by in the alone meaning, use the reflexive herself, not object her.","B":"**Herself** matches the feminine singular subject she; by herself means without help or company.","C":"Himself does not match she.","D":"Themselves does not match the explicitly supplied she in this exercise."}}},{"id":"790667b9-5972-5987-a762-fdc1e34ede64","topicSlug":"reflexive-reciprocal","level":"B1","prompt":"“We measured the garden fence by ____.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"ourselves"},{"id":"B","text":"myself"},{"id":"C","text":"ourself"},{"id":"D","text":"us"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"We requires the plural first-person reflexive **ourselves**.","explanation":"The plural first-person subject we takes **ourselves**.","keywords":["plural-reflexive"],"skill":"plural-reflexive","contextKey":"reflexive-reciprocal-3","fingerprint":"121b936127f416ad0731a67d458e72a96e44563380d2afd2ad40821943a5e348","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reflexive"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["We requires the plural first-person reflexive **ourselves**.","The plural first-person subject we takes **ourselves**.","Choose **ourselves**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The plural first-person subject we takes **ourselves**.","B":"Myself is singular and matches I, not we.","C":"The ordinary plural reflexive for we is ourselves.","D":"The alone/without-help expression needs a reflexive after by."}}},{"id":"7934bfe0-ba1b-5f20-ad55-41e1f4997eda","topicSlug":"reflexive-reciprocal","level":"B1","prompt":"“The two assistants helped each other to measure the garden fence.” What does “each other” show?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Only one assistant received help."},{"id":"B","text":"Neither assistant received help."},{"id":"C","text":"Each assistant helped the other assistant."},{"id":"D","text":"Each assistant helped only themselves."}],"answerId":"C","hint":"A reciprocal action goes **from A to B and from B to A**.","explanation":"**Each other** expresses a reciprocal action between the two assistants.","keywords":["reciprocal-meaning"],"skill":"reciprocal-meaning","contextKey":"reflexive-reciprocal-3","fingerprint":"32b00fdffc1550af2c2c58295394e0a719857965fbacde69c62276cfc7d19f82","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reflexive"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["A reciprocal action goes **from A to B and from B to A**.","**Each other** expresses a reciprocal action between the two assistants.","Choose **Each assistant helped the other assistant.**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The stated reciprocal relationship goes both ways.","B":"This contradicts helped each other.","C":"**Each other** expresses a reciprocal action between the two assistants.","D":"That would be reflexive, not reciprocal."}}},{"id":"1794c9f9-6f07-5486-af07-de330eff8e77","topicSlug":"reflexive-reciprocal","level":"B1","prompt":"“The supervisor asked Sam and ____ to measure the garden fence.” Choose the standard object pronoun for the speaker.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"myself"},{"id":"B","text":"mine"},{"id":"C","text":"me"},{"id":"D","text":"I"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Test the role without the other name: **asked me**.","explanation":"Sam and **me** is the object of asked; removing Sam and leaves asked me.","keywords":["ordinary-object-pronoun"],"skill":"ordinary-object-pronoun","contextKey":"reflexive-reciprocal-3","fingerprint":"1d9f